// Sample rule chunks, paraphrased for tests and demos. NOT the Living Rules Reference.
// Replace with the licensed LRR import under data/private/ (see docs/knowledge-base.md).
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.action_phase","ruleset":"base","title":"Action Phase","text":"Sample paraphrase. Starting with the player holding the lowest initiative strategy card, each player takes one action on their turn: a tactical action, a strategic action, or a component action, or passes. Play continues until every player has passed.","related":["lrr.sample.passing","lrr.sample.tactical_action"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.passing","ruleset":"base","title":"Passing","text":"Sample paraphrase. A player cannot pass until they have performed the strategic action of each strategy card they have. After passing, a player takes no further turns this action phase, though they can still resolve secondary abilities and transactions.","related":["lrr.sample.action_phase"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.tactical_action","ruleset":"base","title":"Tactical Action","text":"Sample paraphrase. A tactical action is resolved in steps: activation, movement, space combat, invasion, production.","related":["lrr.sample.tactical_action.activation","lrr.sample.movement"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.tactical_action.activation","ruleset":"base","title":"Tactical Action: Activation","text":"Sample paraphrase. The active player spends a command token from their tactic pool and places it in a system that does not already contain one of their command tokens. That system is the active system.","parent":"lrr.sample.tactical_action","related":["lrr.sample.command_tokens"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.movement","ruleset":"base","title":"Movement","text":"Sample paraphrase. During movement, the active player may move ships into the active system. Ships cannot move out of a system that contains the moving player's command token. A ship moves a number of systems up to its move value, and may transport ground forces and fighters up to its capacity.","parent":"lrr.sample.tactical_action","related":["lrr.sample.command_tokens","lrr.sample.capacity"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.command_tokens","ruleset":"base","title":"Command Tokens","text":"Sample paraphrase. Players have tactic, fleet and strategy pools. A command token placed in a system marks it activated for that player for the rest of the round.","related":["lrr.sample.tactical_action.activation"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.capacity","ruleset":"base","title":"Capacity","text":"Sample paraphrase. A ship's capacity is how many fighters and ground forces it can transport. Fighters and ground forces in space beyond the capacity of a player's ships in that system are removed.","related":["lrr.sample.movement"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.strategic_action","ruleset":"base","title":"Strategic Action","text":"Sample paraphrase. The active player resolves the primary ability of one of their strategy cards and then exhausts it; other players may then resolve its secondary ability.","related":["lrr.sample.passing"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.timing","ruleset":"base","title":"Timing: When and After","text":"Sample paraphrase. An ability that says 'when' resolves immediately as the triggering event occurs and can change it. An ability that says 'after' resolves immediately after the event. Abilities can only be resolved during their stated timing window.","related":[]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.space_combat","ruleset":"base","title":"Space Combat","text":"Sample paraphrase. If two players have ships in the active system, they resolve space combat in rounds: anti-fighter barrage in the first round only, then each player rolls combat dice and assigns hits to their own ships until one or both players have no ships, or the attacker retreats.","parent":"lrr.sample.tactical_action","related":["lrr.sample.sustain_damage"]}
{"kind":"rule","id":"lrr.sample.sustain_damage","ruleset":"base","title":"Sustain Damage","text":"Sample paraphrase. When a unit with Sustain Damage would be assigned a hit, its owner may place it on its side as damaged to cancel the hit instead. A damaged unit cannot sustain damage again until it is repaired.","related":["lrr.sample.space_combat"]}
